  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The number of isomeric tetraenes (NOT containing sp-hybridized carbon atoms) that can be formed from the following reaction sequence is _____ .</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/d2f64c9a-9cb1-4c7f-981c-9109fedad31f-image.png\" style=\"width: 328px; height: 80px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The anti-addition of hydrogen to an alkyne pi bond occurs when reacted with sodium or lithium metal dissolved in ammonia. This reaction produces a trans-alkene as its product.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/93b4600c-cd6b-4a37-9118-d7f3d031ff97-1636c929-fd14-4607-90d9-447685c5eeed-image.png\" style=\"width: 524px; height: 216px;\" /></p><p>Bromine react with alkene to give anti addition dibromo product. In this case both double bonds will react. In the next reaction elimination of HBr will take place forming tetraene.</p><p>The final tetraene&nbsp;product can show Geometrical isomerism along one double bond only. So, it will have two isomers only.</p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
